Radiographic improvement was seen in this individual’s soft tissue metastasis (Fig.
4b
) although the RECIST assessment was ‘stable disease’ due to the presence of bone metastases.

Notably, UPN388 also had a biopsy-proven prostate cancer metastasis in the pancreas that necessitated stent placement before study entry; this completely resolved after CAR T cell infusion (Fig.
4e
).

Our findings revealed that B7-H3 CAR-T cells effectively suppressed liver tumor growth (Fig.
4d, e
), with a complete response rate of 50% (8/16).
